faqs:
- q: What is sheltered housing?
  a: According to Age UK, sheltered housing, sometimes known as retirement housing, is housing you can buy or rent that has support such as staff, emergency alarms and social activities. It usually includes a scheme manager, a 24-hour emergency alarm, communal areas and social activities, and there is usually a minimum age, such as 55 or 60.
- q: Do you help people move into sheltered housing?
  a: Yes. We help you decide what fits, sort and declutter, pack, move and set up the new flat, planned around your move-in date and the rules of the scheme. We do not recommend or sell retirement properties.
- q: Is sheltered housing the same as a care home?
  a: No. Age UK explains that, unlike care homes, sheltered housing is not inspected or given ratings, and meals and personal care are not usually provided. If you are moving into a care home instead, see our <a href="/care-home-removals/">care home removals</a> page.
- q: Is assisted living the same thing?
  a: Age UK describes assisted living as offering more care options than sheltered housing while still letting you live independently. We help with the practical move into either. We do not give care advice.
- q: How much does it cost to move into sheltered housing?
  a: Chayce packages start at {bronze} for packing and an insured removal. Silver Comfort at {silver} adds sorting and declutter help, a deep clean and unpacking with a coordinator. A Discovery Consultation costs {discovery}. The final price depends on the size of the home and is confirmed in writing before you book.
- q: How do I decide what to take to a smaller flat?
  a: Measure the new rooms first, then sort by category into keep, sell, donate and let go. Our guide to <a href="/blog/downsizing-checklist-what-to-keep-uk/">downsizing</a> and <a href="/blog/planning-furniture-and-floor-plan-for-a-smaller-home/">planning furniture for a smaller home</a> set out the steps.
- q: Can you move me from far away?
  a: Yes. We are based in Northampton and arrange moves across the whole UK. See our <a href="/long-distance-removals-for-older-people/">long-distance removals</a> page.
- q: Is the removal insured?
  a: Yes. Every Chayce removal is fully insured against loss or damage in transit, and the cover is set out in your service agreement before the move begins.
- q: Do you work outside Northampton?
  a: Yes. We are based in Northampton and arrange moves across the whole UK.
